53 ## 5. Quality, final audit, and QA
54 
55 Run `$code-quality` for the affected stacks and dependencies. After all task verdicts and
56 required checks pass, delegate a final read-only audit of the goal's success criteria,
57 integration/wiring, compatibility, and receipts. Verdict APPROVED / ISSUES FOUND.
58 Fix findings, rerun affected checks, and reaudit; maximum three cycles.
59 Only APPROVED permits completion. If the audit changes code, old check receipts for that
60 code no longer certify the fix.
61 
62 Run Profile §9 module QA when a full core gate is requested; otherwise run affected module
63 validators. Run `$ui-qa-orchestrator` for changed UI/flows when Profile §8 applies.
64 For QA issues: create bounded fixes, delegate implementation, rejudge, and rerun the
65 failing QA gate. Never claim a full QA pass from a scoped run.
